From: kosmik2001
Subject: [PATCH] session: start caja with --force-desktop so the desktop is drawn

On this build caja does not draw the desktop in either of the obvious
configurations:

- plain "caja -n" starts during the session's early phase and never takes over
  the desktop (measured on wayfire: no icons until the restart loop happens to
  bring caja up again);
- "caja --force-desktop -n" on the NATIVE wayland backend still draws nothing.

It works under XWayland: GDK_BACKEND=x11 plus --force-desktop -n produces the
desktop on the first start (verified: icons present, no file manager window).
So the session starts it that way.

--- a/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
+++ b/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 restart_while_running mate-panel &
 restart_while_running polkit-mate-authentication-agent-1 &
 restart_while_running mate-notification-daemon &
 restart_while_running mate-settings-daemon &
-restart_while_running caja -n &
+restart_while_running env GDK_BACKEND=x11 caja --force-desktop -n &
 
 #Programs to start once (if we have them), matching Xorg behavior
 nm-applet --indicator &
